Overlay patch 0022: visionOS platform dispatch (Phase 1).
The leetal toolchain sets CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME=visionOS for
PLATFORM=SIMULATOR_VISIONOS/VISIONOS, but the whole tree (upstream LUS +
our iOS overlay CMake) dispatches on STREQUAL "iOS" at 16+ sites. Rather
than patching every site, flip CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME back to "iOS" right
after project(): by then compilers, sysroot (xrsimulator/xros), and
Xcode's SDKROOT are locked, so the flip only affects dispatch
conditionals. The real visionOS-ness continues to come from the SDK
(TARGET_OS_VISION=1 in TargetConditionals). SOH_VISIONOS stays a cache
var for genuinely vision-specific deltas (device family, plist).
Deployment target: CMake then emits IPHONEOS_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET, which
Xcode ignores for xros — build-vision-sim.sh compensates with
CMAKE_XCODE_ATTRIBUTE_XROS_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET=2.0. No-op for iOS builds
(condition never true).
rev5: language-scope the top-level -fno-fast-math genex — plain
add_compile_options feeds it to EVERY compiler the Xcode generator
invokes, and swiftc (the D-030 SwiftUI entry) hard-errors on unknown
C driver flags.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -7,6 +7,17 @@
 set(CMAKE_OSX_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET "10.15" CACHE STRING "Minimum OS X deployment version")
 
 project(Ship VERSION 9.2.3 LANGUAGES C CXX)
+
+# SOH_IOS (overlay 0022): visionOS builds (PLATFORM=SIMULATOR_VISIONOS /
+# VISIONOS) dispatch as iOS throughout the tree. Compilers and SDK are
+# already fixed by the toolchain at this point; only the STREQUAL "iOS"
+# conditionals care. TARGET_OS_VISION (from the xros SDK) remains the
+# source-level discriminator.
+if(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "visionOS")
+    set(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME "iOS")
+    set(IOS 1)
+    set(SOH_VISIONOS 1)
+endif()
 include(CMake/soh-cvars.cmake)
 include(CMake/lus-cvars.cmake)
 set(SPDLOG_LEVEL_TRACE 0)
@@ -140,8 +151,11 @@
 # Enforce strict, deterministic IEEE-754 floating-point to match N64 (MIPS) semantics.
 # Never enable fast-math, and disable FMA contraction: the R4300 CPU and RSP have no
 # fused multiply-add, so contracting mul+add into an FMA produces extra precision.
-add_compile_options($<$<CXX_COMPILER_ID:GNU,Clang,AppleClang>:-fno-fast-math>)
-add_compile_options($<$<CXX_COMPILER_ID:GNU,Clang,AppleClang>:-ffp-contract=off>)
+# SOH_IOS (overlay 0022 rev5): scope to C-family languages — the Xcode
+# generator otherwise passes these to swiftc (visionOS SwiftUI entry),
+# which hard-errors on unknown C driver flags.
+add_compile_options($<$<AND:$<COMPILE_LANGUAGE:C,CXX,OBJC,OBJCXX>,$<CXX_COMPILER_ID:GNU,Clang,AppleClang>>:-fno-fast-math>)
+add_compile_options($<$<AND:$<COMPILE_LANGUAGE:C,CXX,OBJC,OBJCXX>,$<CXX_COMPILER_ID:GNU,Clang,AppleClang>>:-ffp-contract=off>)
 add_compile_options($<$<CXX_COMPILER_ID:MSVC>:/fp:precise>)
 add_compile_options($<$<CXX_COMPILER_ID:MSVC>:/fp:except->)
 
--- a/libultraship/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/libultraship/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -19,6 +19,15 @@
 
 project(libultraship LANGUAGES C CXX)
 
+# SOH_IOS (overlay 0022): this project() re-ran the toolchain, resetting
+# CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME to visionOS — re-flip so the tree keeps dispatching as
+# iOS (see the top-level CMakeLists hunk).
+if(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "visionOS")
+    set(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME "iOS")
+    set(IOS 1)
+    set(SOH_VISIONOS 1)
+endif()
+
 if (CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "Darwin" OR CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "iOS")
     enable_language(OBJCXX)
     set(CMAKE_OBJC_FLAGS "${CMAKE_OBJC_FLAGS} -fobjc-arc")
@@ -75,6 +84,15 @@
 # === Platform Specific Configuration ===
 if(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "iOS")
     include(cmake/ios-toolchain-populate.cmake)
+    # SOH_IOS (overlay 0022): the toolchain include above re-ran leetal's
+    # platform init IN THIS SCOPE, resetting CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME to visionOS
+    # again — re-flip a third time so src/ (compile definitions, __IOS__)
+    # dispatches as iOS.
+    if(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "visionOS")
+        set(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME "iOS")
+        set(IOS 1)
+        set(SOH_VISIONOS 1)
+    endif()
 endif()
 
